# Line endings for everything in this directory that an interpreter reads.
#
# These scripts are bind-mounted from the Windows host into the harness and run
# there, so Git's checkout conversion applies to the file the container runs.
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) Git rewrites LF to CRLF, and:
#
#   /usr/local/bin/init-token.sh: 14: set: Illegal option -   (/bin/sh = dash)
#   env: 'python3\r': No such file or directory               (direct ./script.py)
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf for these files, so a clone behaves the same
# on Windows and Linux whatever the local Git setting is.
#
# The rule lives next to the files because the repository root is not writable
# from inside the container; docs/gitattributes.txt carries the repository-wide
# copy for the host.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
